  "name": "Parthenon",
  "_about": "THE PARTHENON, Athens (447-432 BC), from the same components as the Temple of Hephaestus and at its real size: a stylobate 30.88 x 69.5m on steps half a metre high, 8 x 17 Doric columns 10.43m tall and 1.91m thick, the entablature 3.29m deep with its triglyphs (ninety-six of them, one geometry drawn ninety-six times), the naos with six-column porches at both ends -- the pronaos before the door and the opisthodomos behind -- the coffered ceiling, and the low gable whose ends are the pediments.",
